# ISL → English (DeepMind-style keypoints + T5)

```
video -> MediaPipe keypoints -> conv projector -> T5 encoder-decoder -> English text
```

## Run order (VS Code terminal)

```bash
python -m venv .venv && .venv\Scripts\activate      # Windows  (source .venv/bin/activate on Mac/Linux)
pip install -r requirements.txt
# for GPU install the CUDA build of torch from pytorch.org first

# 0. download dataset from Kaggle and unzip to e.g. D:/isl_dataset
python extract_keypoints.py --data D:/isl_dataset --inspect     # check labels look right
python extract_keypoints.py --data D:/isl_dataset --out features

python train.py --features features --split seen --out runs/seen
python train.py --features features --split unseen --n-unseen 10 --out runs/unseen

python infer_live.py --ckpt runs/seen/best.pt
```

## Reading the numbers
- `exact_acc` / `snapped_acc` on `--split seen` = closed-set accuracy (same 100 sentences, new videos).
- `--split unseen` = real translation test on sentences never seen. Expect it to be much lower.
- Report both in your project/LinkedIn post. Without signer IDs the split is not signer-independent.

## If labels look wrong
`--inspect` prints 8 sample paths with their labels. If your dataset has a CSV (video -> sentence):
`--csv labels.csv --csv-key <video column> --csv-text <sentence column>`

## Upgrades
- `--model google/mt5-small` or `google/byt5-small`
- pretrain on a bigger ISL set (iSign) first, then fine-tune on ISL-CSLTR